# Python: always use uv

This repo is a **uv-managed** project ([`pyproject.toml`](pyproject.toml), [`.python-version`](.python-version)).

## Required (agents + humans)

- Install deps: **`uv sync`** (or `make uv-sync`) — never `pip install`.
- Run anything Python: **`uv run …`** — never `python`, `python3`, `python -m`, or `.venv/bin/…`.
- Tests: **`uv run pytest …`** or **`make test-agent`**.
- Brain (local): **`uv run brain-dev`** or **`make agent-brain`** (port **8002** default).
- One-liners: **`uv run python -c "…"`** — not `python3 -c`.

After editing **`.env`**, restart brain: `make brain-restart` (kills :8002, then `uv run brain-dev`).

## Project entry points (console scripts)

| Command | Role |
|---------|------|
| `uv run brain-dev` | FastAPI brain with reload |
| `uv run datasyn-api` | Brain without reload |
| `uv run pytest tests/ -q` | Unit tests |

Prefer **`make agent-dev`**. Images: **`make build-agent`**, **`make build-ui`**, **`make push`** (see `INSTALL.md`).

## Forbidden on the host

- `python -m uvicorn …`
- `pip install …`
- `python3 agent/…`
- `.venv/bin/brain-dev` (even if `.venv` exists — use `uv run brain-dev`)

Docker **build** uses `uv pip install --system` ([`Dockerfile`](Dockerfile)); runtime in the image uses the `uvicorn` entrypoint on PATH. Local dev always uses **`uv run`**.

## VS Code / Cursor tasks

Use [`.vscode/tasks.json`](.vscode/tasks.json): **uv sync**, **brain-dev (uv only)**, **agent-dev (uv + Vite)**.
